  "description" : "This dataset contains the total fall enrollment headcount and full-time equivalent (FTE) counts for undergraduate and graduate students at all public Massachusetts institutions of higher education since 2014. Data are disaggregated by the year of fall term, segment, institution, and student attributes such as enrollment level, enrollment status, race/ethnicity, and gender.\n\nThis dataset is 1 of 2 datasets that is also published in the interactive\n<a href=\"https://www.mass.edu/datacenter/factbook/fallenrollment.asp\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Fall Enrollment dashboard</a> on the Department of Higher Education Data Center:\n\n1) <a href=\"https://educationtocareer.data.mass.gov/College-and-Career/Public-Postsecondary-Fall-Enrollment/gzpm-dvfd/about_data\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Public Postsecondary Fall Enrollment: Detail</a>\n2) <a href=\"https://educationtocareer.data.mass.gov/College-and-Career/Public-Postsecondary-Fall-Enrollment-by-Race-and-G/v4jy-wi85/about_data\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Public Postsecondary Fall Enrollment: Summary</a>\n\nRelated datasets:\n1) <a href=\"https://educationtocareer.data.mass.gov/dataset/Public-Postsecondary-Annual-Enrollment/j7yp-crt6/about_data\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Public Postsecondary Annual Enrollment: Detail</a>\n2) <a href=\"https://educationtocareer.data.mass.gov/College-and-Career/Public-Postsecondary-Annual-Enrollment-by-Race-and/hx2h-9z86/about_data\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Public Postsecondary Annual Enrollment: Summary</a>\n\nNotes:\n- Data appear as reported to the Massachusetts Department of Higher Education.\n- Figures published here may vary from those of individual institutions due to differences in calculation methodologies.\n- Enrollment can also be measured as full time equivalent (FTE), which is calculated based on the total number of credits carried by enrolled students. In the fall term, 15 undergraduate credits = 1 FTE. For graduate students, 12 credits = 1 FTE at state universities, while at UMass campuses 9 credits = 1 FTE (except for first-professional degree programs which use a 15 credits FTE-standard).\n- The FTE column is formatted for display. Use the FTE_RAW column to calculate accurate aggregations.",
